dn-survey>
            <h1>CSS properties</h1>
             <section class=3D"content-section">
   =20
    <p>A <a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS">CSS</=
a> <strong><em>property</em></strong> is a parameter used in a <a href=3D"h=
ttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Syntax/Introduction#=
css_declarations">CSS declaration</a> that lets you style certain aspects o=
f selected elements.
For example, the <a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CS=
S/Reference/Properties/opacity"><code>opacity</code></a> property is used t=
o set the opacity of a selected element, allowing you to control if content=
 behind that element is visible:</p>
<mdn-code-example class=3D"brush: css notranslate"><template shadowmode=3D"=
open"><!---->
      <div class=3D"code-example">
        <div class=3D"example-header">
          <span class=3D"language-name"><!--?lit$729108603$-->css</span>
          <mdn-copy-button variant=3D"secondary"><template shadowmode=3D"op=
en"><!----><mdn-button variant=3D"secondary"><template shadowmode=3D"open">=
<!---->
        <button class=3D"button" part=3D"button" aria-labelledby=3D"label-z=
9yh34hq6ja" data-variant=3D"secondary">
          <!--?lit$729108603$--><!----><!----><!---->
    <span class=3D"label" part=3D"label" id=3D"label-z9yh34hq6ja"><!--?lit$=
729108603$--><slot></slot></span>
  <!---->
        </button>
      </template><!--?lit$729108603$-->Copy</mdn-button></template></mdn-co=
py-button>
          <!--?lit$729108603$-->
        </div>
        <pre class=3D"brush: css notranslate"><code><!--?lit$729108603$--><=
span class=3D"token comment">/* Set 0.8 opacity on &lt;img&gt; elements */<=
/span>
<span class=3D"token selector">img</span> <span class=3D"token punctuation"=
>{</span>
  <span class=3D"token property">opacity</span><span class=3D"token punctua=
tion">:</span> 0.8<span class=3D"token punctuation">;</span>
<span class=3D"token punctuation">}</span>
</code></pre>
      </div>
    </template></mdn-code-example>
<p>Each property has a name (e.g., <code>opacity</code>), a value (e.g., <c=
ode>0.8</code>), and a defined behavior on the rendering of the document.
CSS also defines shorthand properties, so you can specify multiple related =
properties in a single declaration.
For example, the <a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CS=
S/Reference/Properties/margin"><code>margin</code></a> property is a shorth=
and for <a href=3D"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Referen=
